# Page objects (Playwright)

## Where locators live

Locators and interactions belong in `tests/pages/*`; specs wire flows and call `expect`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/e2e/browse.spec.ts
const browse = new BrowsePage(page);
await browse.open();
await browse.selectSort('price-desc');
await expect(browse.plantsCountHeading).toBeVisible();
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — locator in the spec
await page.getByLabel('Sort by').selectOption('price-desc');
```

## Locator order

Prefer `getByRole`, then `getByLabel`, then `getByText`. Do not use CSS or XPath in page objects.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/BrowsePage.ts
this.sortBy = page.getByLabel('Sort by');
this.plantsCountHeading = page.getByRole('heading', { level: 2, name: /\d+ plants/ });
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — tests/a11y/helpers/scan.ts (not a page object pattern)
return page.locator(selector).first();
```

## Actions return value

Action methods perform one user step. Return `void` or `this` / the next page object — never assert.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
async selectSort(value: string): Promise<BrowsePage> {
  await this.sortBy.selectOption(value);
  return this;
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — assertion inside a page object
async selectSort(value: string) {
  await this.sortBy.selectOption(value);
  await expect(this.plantsCountHeading).toBeVisible();
}
```

## Assertions stay in the spec

Page objects expose `Locator`s; only `*.spec.ts` files import `expect` for UI checks.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/e2e/browse.spec.ts
await expect(browse.firstPlantCardHeading).toContainText(MOST_EXPENSIVE_NAME);
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — would belong in a page object (never do this)
await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { level: 3 })).toContainText(name);
```
